<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-U.S. BEAT ITALY 4-2 IN WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-U.S. BEAT ITALY 4-2 IN WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results at the world ice hockey championships on Wednesday:</p>
<p>Pool B (in Turku)</p>
<p>United States 4 Italy 2 (0-1 1-0 3-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>United States - Chris Tancill (25:11), Dan Plante (40:18)</p>
<p>Marty McInnis (50:09), Paul Ranheim (59:34)</p>
<p>Italy - Chris Bartolone (3:07), Dino Felicetti (45:24)</p>
<p>Penalties:</p>
<p>United States 18 minutes, Italy 20</p>
<p>Pool A</p>
<p>Russia 5 France 4 (2-0 2-3 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Russia - Alexei Chupin (11:53), Anatoly Fedotov (18:51), Dmitry Krasotkin (21:06), Alexander Prokopyev (22:47), Alexander Barkov (56:20).</p>
<p>France - Roger Dube (29:06, 36:56), Pierre Allard (30:20), Arnaud Briand (55:59).</p>
<p>Penalties: Russia 14 minutes, France 14 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 12,708.</p>
</text>
